    <string name="intro_reactancia">Calculates the reactance of a coil (XL = 2πfL) and of a capacitor (XC = 1 / 2πfC) at a given frequency.</string>
    <string name="intro_impedancia_rx">Calculates the impedance of a series load from its resistance and reactance, with the angle and power factor.</string>
    <string name="intro_joule">Calculates the heat a resistance dissipates by the Joule effect: Q = I² × R × t.</string>
    <string name="intro_suma_resistencias">Calculates the equivalent resistance of up to 6 resistors in series or parallel.</string>
    <string name="intro_suma_condensadores">Calculates the equivalent capacitance of up to 6 capacitors in series or parallel.</string>
    <string name="intro_resonancia">Calculates the resonant frequency of an LC circuit: f₀ = 1 / (2π√LC).</string>
    <string name="intro_potencia_condensador">Calculates the reactive power a capacitor delivers at a given voltage: Q = U² × 2πf × C.</string>
    <string name="intro_divisor_tension">Calculates the output voltage of an unloaded resistive divider.</string>
    <string name="intro_divisor_corriente">Calculates how current splits between two parallel resistors.</string>
    <string name="intro_zener">Calculates the series resistor of a Zener regulator and the power they dissipate.</string>
    <string name="intro_reducir_tension">Calculates the series resistor that drops the voltage for a constant-current load.</string>
    <string name="intro_led">Calculates the current-limiting resistor for one or more LEDs in series, and its power.</string>
    <string name="intro_antena">Calculates the wavelength and the lengths of half-wave and quarter-wave antennas.</string>
